=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: sshswitch
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** The Layer 3 bridge interface `br_v5` on `sshswitch` — the VLAN 5 Switched Virtual Interface (SVI) that provides the default gateway `10.5.0.254/24` for Campus 2 VLAN 5 hosts.

**Mechanism:** `sshswitch` is a Layer 3 managed switch that bridges tagged VLAN sub-interfaces (`eth0.5`, `bond0.5`) into a routed SVI bridge (`br_v5`). The IP `10.5.0.254` is configured on `br_v5`, which is the default gateway for pc1, pc2, and dc_pc5. Because `br_v5` is administratively DOWN, the switch never processes ARP requests arriving on the VLAN 5 segment, so no ARP reply is sent for `10.5.0.254`. All three VLAN 5 hosts record the gateway as ARP `FAILED` and generate local `Destination Host Unreachable` ICMP errors for every off-subnet packet.

**Localization:** `sshswitch`, interface `br_v5` — state `DOWN`, zero carrier-changes (never came up). The peer VLAN 6 SVI (`br_v6`, IP `10.6.0.254`) is `UP,LOWER_UP` and fully operational, which is why pc3 and pc4 are unaffected. Both physical member sub-interfaces (`bond0.5` and `eth0.5`) are UP — only the bridge itself is shut down.

**Root cause:** The VLAN 5 SVI bridge `br_v5` on `sshswitch` was administratively taken down (`ip link set br_v5 down`), silencing the VLAN 5 gateway and cutting all inter-subnet reachability for VLAN 5 hosts.

**Fix:** Run `ip link set br_v5 up` on `sshswitch` to restore the VLAN 5 SVI. No hardware changes are needed; all sub-interfaces are already UP.
=== END ===